{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1087", "sample_idx": 20, "model_name": "meta/llama-4-maverick-17b-128e-instruct", "content": "the social network is a 2010 film directed by david fincher that tells the story of the founding of facebook, the social media giant. the movie is based on the book \"the accidental billionaires\" by ben mezrich, which chronicles the rise of mark zuckerberg, the co-founder and ceo of facebook.\n\nthe film begins with mark zuckerberg (played by jesse eisenberg), a sophomore at harvard university, who is dumped by his girlfriend, erica albright (played by raisa wolfe). in a fit of anger and sadness, mark creates a website called \"facemash\" that allows users to compare the photos of two harvard students and vote on which one is more attractive. the site becomes an instant hit, but also gets mark into trouble with the university administration.\n\nlater, mark is approached by twin brothers cameron and tyler winklevoss (played by armie hammer), who are members of the harvard rowing team and are looking to create a social networking site for harvard students. mark agrees to help them, but eventually becomes more interested in creating his own site, which he calls \"thefacebook\".\n\nas the site gains popularity, mark is joined by his college roommates and fellow students eduardo saverin (played by andrew garfield), dustin moskovitz (played by joseph mazello), and chris hughes (played by patrick mapel). however, tensions arise between mark and eduardo, who is initially the chief financial officer of the company, over issues of ownership and control.\n\nthe film is known for its witty and insightful dialogue, which explores themes of friendship, betrayal, and the consequences of success. the cast delivers strong performances, with jesse eisenberg standing out as the complex and often unlikeable mark zuckerberg.\n\none of the strengths of the film is its ability to capture the spirit of the early days of facebook and the culture of harvard university at the time. the movie's portrayal of the privileged and entitled world of harvard's elite is both fascinating and disturbing, and raises important questions about the nature of ambition and the costs of success.\n\nthe film's score, composed by trent reznor and atticus ross, is also noteworthy, featuring a haunting and atmospheric soundtrack that perfectly complements the tone of the movie.\n\noverall, the social network is a compelling and thought-provoking film that offers a nuanced and insightful look at the founding of facebook and the complex personalities involved. while some of the details of the film have been disputed by those involved in the creation of facebook, the movie remains a fascinating and engaging portrayal of the rise of one of the most influential companies of the 21st century.", "logprobs": [{"token": "the", "logprob": -0.8832516670227051}, {"token": " social", "logprob": -0.0003196682082489133}, {"token": " network", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " is", "logprob": -0.008614758029580116}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -9.536738616588991e-07}, {"token": " ", "logprob": -1.6641584634780884}, {"token": "201", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "0", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " film", "logprob": -0.0005800233921036124}, {"token": " directed", "logprob": -0.0005529781919904053}, {"token": " by", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " david", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " fin", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "cher", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " that", "logprob": -0.1297278106212616}, {"token": " tells", "logprob": -0.0013222293928265572}, {"token": " the", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " story", "logprob": -5.960462772236497e-07}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -4.768370445162873e-07}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -6.198863957251888e-06}, {"token": " founding", "logprob": -2.038458114839159e-05}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -0.0005529781919904053}, {"token": " facebook", "logprob": -0.00020346954988781363}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -0.6931478977203369}, {"token": " the", "log